Corpus provenance and licensing
================================

The code in this repository is MIT licensed (see LICENSE).

The caselaw corpus under `corpus/` is a separate matter. It consists of United
States court opinions, which are not subject to copyright, retrieved from the
Caselaw Access Project (https://static.case.law). Every stored opinion records
its own `source_url` and retrieval date in its JSON sidecar; all 352 opinions in
this repository resolve to static.case.law.

Reporters still under copyright are deliberately excluded: West's Supreme Court
Reporter (`S. Ct.`) and the Lawyers' Edition (`L. Ed.`, `L. Ed. 2d`) appear
nowhere in the corpus, and continuous integration asserts their absence on every
run rather than relying on this note.
